-- Arena ladder chat (BT-154, Arena/ArenaChat.cpp): what the bots of a team say in the General channel about a new team, a
-- win streak, a streak they ended, a climb in the ranking and a close rivalry. Key '<name>_<personality>' (quiet, friendly,
-- joker, grumpy) is a variant of '<name>'; a bot uses its own variant in 6 of 10 cases and the plain pool otherwise.
-- Placeholders: %team, %opp, %rating, %streak, %record. The module has a default line in code for every key, so the chat
-- works before this file is loaded. Safe to run again: the rows of these names are replaced.

DELETE FROM `ai_playerbot_texts` WHERE `name` LIKE 'arn\_%';

